{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From this [G]valley they say you are [D]going
We will [G]miss your bright eyes and sweet [D]smile
For they [G]say you are taking the [C]sunshine
That has [D]brightened our pathway a-[G]while
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [D]love me
Do not [G]hasten to bid me a-[D]dieu
But re-[G]member the Red River [C]Valley
And the [D]one who has loved you so [G]true
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Won't you [G]think of the valley you're [D]leaving
Oh how [G]lonely, how sad it will [D]be
Oh, just [G]think of the fond heart you're [C]breaking
And the [D]grief you are causing to [G]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
